; Winter roofs -- snow.
;
; HAND-AUTHORED, not measured. Christmas's values were tried first and read as
; cyan paint on our roof tiles -- it collapses every outdoor palette onto one
; icy ramp, which works there because its tileset is redrawn as snow.
;
; These aim at settled snow: bright and slightly blue, with a shadowed second
; colour so the roof's own shading still reads. Eve derived with the roof
; day->eve fit (R x0.850  G x0.750  B x0.742), which reproduces vanilla's eve
; roof exactly.
;
; The table is per-group anyway, so giving Olivine a different snow tint from
; Goldenrod is a pure data edit -- no code change. Do that if a flat roof colour
; reads as wrong on our unmodified tiles.
;
; Colours 1 and 2 only; colours 0 and 3 come from bg_tiles.pal.

; group 0 (unused)
	RGB 24,28,31, 14,18,26 ; morn/day
	RGB 13,14,22, 07,09,16 ; nite
	RGB 20,21,23, 12,14,19 ; eve

; group 1 (Olivine)
